# Collected-count baseline for scripts/ci_guard.py: the API suites (backend/tests/test_*.py and
# backend/tests/backend_test.py) must run at least this many tests to a verdict, with zero plain
# skips, or CI fails. Expected failures (pytest.mark.xfail) do not count, so xfailing a test lowers
# the count exactly as deleting it would.
#
# Method (2026-10-13, main @ 880a5f1): the API modules skip at import time without ADMIN_EMAIL,
# ADMIN_PASSWORD and DEMO_USERS_PASSWORD, so `python -m pytest --collect-only -q` counts nothing
# offline. Counted instead with
#     grep -c '^\s*def test_' backend/tests/test_*.py backend/tests/backend_test.py
# (none of these files parametrizes, so one def is one collected test):
#     backend_test.py 31, test_flagship.py 33, test_iteration6.py 17, test_iteration7.py 14,
#     test_layout_roadmap.py 14, test_phase1_lifecycle.py 17                      -> 126
# Carve-out: 126 minus the Emergent-storage round trip
# (test_phase1_lifecycle.py::TestAttachments::test_upload_list_download_delete), deselected in CI until
# storage has a local backend. storage.py talks only to the Emergent-hosted object store and needs
# EMERGENT_LLM_KEY; CI has no such secret (fork PRs have none, and a real key would write to the real
# store), so the upload answers 502. Deselected, not skipped, so the zero-skip rule above stays honest.
# Restore 126 once a local/in-memory backend is selected when the key is unset (wave 2).  -> 125
# test_concurrency.py adds 2 tests that are xfail(strict) until the wave-2 lost-update fix; they are
# collected (127 with the carve-out) but not counted. When that fix drops the markers, raise this by 2.
# tests/unit runs in its own CI step and is never counted here. Raise the number whenever API tests are
# added so the floor follows main.
125
